WEBVTT

00:01.991 --> 00:05.101
Lucie-goosie, Daddy's here.

00:05.101 --> 00:06.621
Up, up you go!

00:08.621 --> 00:11.021
<i>Oh, she's adorable.</i>

00:11.021 --> 00:15.271
<i>Could there be anything else on 
earth as cute as a smiling Lucie?</i>

00:15.551 --> 00:19.691
<i>If angels exist, 
my little girl must be one.</i>

00:20.001 --> 00:21.881
Hey, Rudeus.

00:21.881 --> 00:25.281
I can rock her, you know. 
I am her wet nurse.

00:25.281 --> 00:29.341
I wish you wouldn't try to take 
my moments of bliss, Suzanne.

00:29.341 --> 00:32.781
Well, if you want to do it 
yourself, I won't stop you.

00:32.781 --> 00:35.281
What man wouldn't want to?

00:35.281 --> 00:38.181
My husband sure doesn't.

00:38.181 --> 00:42.391
Maybe Timothy needs to think 
more about fatherhood.

00:43.561 --> 00:45.171
Right, Lucie?

00:43.951 --> 00:47.091
Huh... You're a funny one.

00:47.401 --> 00:52.241
Anyway, I had no idea 
you moved to Sharia.

00:52.241 --> 00:53.681
Same here.

00:53.681 --> 00:57.501
I never thought you'd get married 
and even have a daughter.

00:58.461 --> 01:01.111
The party split up, right?

01:01.111 --> 01:05.131
Yeah. A little while after 
we parted ways with you.

01:05.131 --> 01:09.901
At our level, losing one 
member takes a toll.

01:12.451 --> 01:14.661
What happened to Sara?

01:14.661 --> 01:16.351
You really want to know?

01:16.351 --> 01:18.071
Well, I guess.

01:18.481 --> 01:21.261
She's still adventuring.

01:22.361 --> 01:25.721
If you're going to talk to her, 
the sooner, the better.

01:25.721 --> 01:28.501
You never know when an 
adventurer is going to die.

01:30.331 --> 01:34.251
No, I don't have anything 
much to say to her.

01:35.021 --> 01:36.271
Is that so?

01:37.731 --> 01:40.101
Pardon me, Master Rudeus.

01:40.101 --> 01:44.701
Her Ladyship seemed concerned about 
Miss Lucie, so I brought her here.

01:44.701 --> 01:48.561
Mom, Lucie is as happy 
and healthy as ever.

01:52.571 --> 01:55.831
You love your grandma, 
don't you, Lucie-goosie?

02:05.481 --> 02:08.381
Master Rudeus, if I may.

02:10.711 --> 02:13.211
There, there. What's the matter?

02:13.561 --> 02:15.701
Did you make a mess in your diaper?

02:17.451 --> 02:19.521
Well, I guess she's hungry.

02:22.561 --> 02:27.351
<i>Could she have noticed 
that Lucie wanted milk?</i>

02:28.091 --> 02:31.641
<i>I hope that's another 
sign that she's recovering.</i>

02:41.901 --> 02:45.321
Thank you for accepting this job.

02:45.321 --> 02:48.411
I wouldn't refuse a request from you.

02:48.631 --> 02:54.041
Still, guarding the princess of Ranoa? 
I always knew you were special.

02:54.041 --> 02:56.261
No, things just worked out this way.

02:56.591 --> 03:00.751
<i>Apparently, Ranoan royals are 
required to make a journey</i>

03:00.751 --> 03:04.181
<i>to prove themselves before 
they come of age.</i>

03:04.501 --> 03:08.021
<i>It's not much of a journey, 
just a tour of the local shrines,</i>

03:08.021 --> 03:11.101
<i>but they have to arrange 
for their own protection.</i>

03:11.921 --> 03:16.451
An adventurer from the party that's 
been guarding her got sick, right?

03:16.451 --> 03:20.371
Yes. We'll be filling in for her.

03:20.891 --> 03:24.021
I heard something about 
Princess Ariel joining us.

03:24.021 --> 03:27.831
I believe she wants to get to 
know the princess of Ranoa.

03:27.831 --> 03:31.691
I'm impressed she's willing to go 
into a monster-infested forest,

03:31.691 --> 03:34.211
even if it is to make connections.

03:34.211 --> 03:39.571
Personally, I'm more
worried about having

03:39.571 --> 03:42.581
<i>two</i> royals to guard now.

03:44.201 --> 03:48.341
So, having you along will 
take a weight off my mind.

03:48.681 --> 03:51.171
You've got nothing to worry 
about while I'm around.

03:51.171 --> 03:52.801
I'm counting on it.

03:53.021 --> 03:59.031
<b>III</b>

03:53.021 --> 03:59.031
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

03:53.021 --> 03:59.031
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

04:01.491 --> 04:04.191
My! Do you have them in Asura, too, then?

04:04.191 --> 04:07.441
Yes. We keep gardens inside our castles.

04:07.701 --> 04:10.901
I suppose that's the 
same everywhere, then!

04:11.721 --> 04:12.951
How delightful!

04:13.981 --> 04:17.071
Who are you? Name yourselves.

04:17.071 --> 04:18.501
It's nice to meet you.

04:18.501 --> 04:21.191
I'm called Roxy Migurdia Greyrat.

04:21.191 --> 04:22.961
I am Rudeus Greyrat.

04:23.241 --> 04:29.721
Dame Grace, these are the pair I told you 
will be guarding Her Royal Highness.

04:30.391 --> 04:33.041
Oh, so you're the ones.

04:33.641 --> 04:35.481
I've heard the whole story.

04:35.481 --> 04:37.731
I'm Grace, a knight.

04:37.731 --> 04:39.281
We're glad to have you today.

04:39.681 --> 04:43.371
We heard that there would be 
other adventurers as well.

04:43.371 --> 04:46.691
A party called Amazon Ace.

04:46.691 --> 04:49.421
They should be back any moment now.

04:48.691 --> 04:50.571
Stop being unreasonable!

04:50.571 --> 04:53.871
Unreasonable?! Did you forget 
what happened last time?!

04:53.871 --> 04:57.751
Tina and Melanie nearly died because 
those idiots didn't stick to the plan!

04:57.751 --> 04:59.571
I don't want any part of this!

04:59.571 --> 05:02.541
What do you want me to do? 
The job is what it is.

05:02.541 --> 05:06.351
I'm better off working alone 
than with some weirdos!

05:06.351 --> 05:12.301
I like to think I know my limits too well 
to let you watch my back alone.

05:12.301 --> 05:16.281
You need to learn to work with 
anyone you're teamed up with.

05:16.611 --> 05:17.991
It may not seem important now,

05:17.991 --> 05:21.301
but you won't be able to stick 
with the same party forever.

05:28.421 --> 05:29.741
You're the one they got?

05:29.741 --> 05:31.571
Who's he? Someone you know?

05:31.571 --> 05:33.201
Something like that.

05:37.471 --> 05:41.721
<i>Sara. I doubt I'll ever 
be able to forget her.</i>

05:42.151 --> 05:47.451
<i>She's crude and headstrong, 
but she's not stupid.</i>

05:47.991 --> 05:52.671
<i>We took on a bunch of jobs together, 
and she ended up falling for me.</i>

05:53.331 --> 05:55.531
<i>At least, I'm pretty sure she did.</i>

05:56.271 --> 06:00.101
<i>I, on the other hand, never really 
figured out how I felt about her.</i>

06:00.571 --> 06:05.031
<i>Our relationship progressed and then 
ended before I could be certain.</i>

06:05.491 --> 06:07.571
<i>That's right. It ended.</i>

06:07.941 --> 06:10.741
<i>I was never going to see her again.</i>

06:11.661 --> 06:13.911
<i>Or so I thought.</i>

06:15.611 --> 06:18.871
Alyssa! Sara! Two went your way!

06:19.111 --> 06:22.421
Let the great protection of fire 
be on the place thou seekest.

06:22.681 --> 06:25.301
I call the bold heat of 
a torch here and now.

06:25.301 --> 06:26.851
Fireball!

06:30.801 --> 06:33.931
Let a smoldering spark 
incinerate tremendous bounty!

06:34.211 --> 06:35.881
Flamethrower!

06:44.821 --> 06:46.181
Well now.

06:50.391 --> 06:52.721
Are you having any trouble over there?

06:52.721 --> 06:53.781
I'm fine!

07:05.201 --> 07:07.231
I'll be damned.

07:07.231 --> 07:09.921
That was one easy win.

07:09.921 --> 07:13.401
They do say a teacher cleared 
the Teleporter Labyrinth.

07:13.401 --> 07:15.531
I guess it's true.

07:15.531 --> 07:19.171
The way you balanced offensive and 
healing magic left me in awe!

07:19.171 --> 07:23.011
I never dreamed that anyone could put 
theory into practice so perfectly!

07:23.011 --> 07:24.611
Look who's talking.

07:24.611 --> 07:28.341
What happened to, "I can't believe 
I'm stuck with this little kid"?

07:28.341 --> 07:30.491
I'm so sorry for running my mouth!

07:30.491 --> 07:33.701
I... I don't mind. 
It happens all the time.

07:33.701 --> 07:38.801
<i>It sure is nice seeing people treat 
Roxy with the reverence she deserves.</i>

07:39.631 --> 07:41.971
<i>That's my master, you know?</i>

07:46.691 --> 07:50.941
Okay, we need to have food ready 
before the princesses get back!

07:50.941 --> 07:51.801
Listen, Rudeus—

07:51.801 --> 07:53.771
Oh, I'll handle the cooking!

07:53.771 --> 07:55.941
Since I'm not much use fighting and all!

07:55.941 --> 07:57.421
Huh? But—

07:57.421 --> 07:58.841
I won't let you down!

07:58.841 --> 08:00.921
I might not look it, but I'm a good cook!

08:00.921 --> 08:03.141
So, she used to be his woman?

08:03.551 --> 08:06.021
Do you know what happened between them?

08:06.021 --> 08:08.321
I've got a general idea.

08:10.081 --> 08:13.191
We may run into more 
monsters on our way back.

08:13.471 --> 08:16.701
If there's anything else you'd 
like done, just say the word.

08:13.561 --> 08:16.071
I'd like to have everyone focused.

08:18.991 --> 08:21.941
The service at the shrine 
went well, then?

08:21.941 --> 08:22.951
Yes.

08:22.951 --> 08:27.171
With your help, I believe I can finish 
my pilgrimage here in comfort.

08:27.171 --> 08:29.001
I'm delighted to hear it.

08:29.001 --> 08:33.411
Dearest Sister! Would you mind terribly 
teaching me magic on our way?

08:33.411 --> 08:35.201
Well, I don't see why not.

08:35.201 --> 08:36.581
Hooray!

08:36.581 --> 08:37.961
Thank you so much, Dearest Sister!

08:37.961 --> 08:40.481
Um... Why are you calling me that?

08:42.411 --> 08:45.211
<i>It stings seeing how much 
warmer a reception Roxy gets.</i>

08:45.211 --> 08:46.831
<i>I wish I could join the fun.</i>

08:47.261 --> 08:50.611
<i>And I'd love it if Roxy called 
me "Dearest Brother."</i>

08:50.611 --> 08:53.181
Rudy, you two know each other, right?

08:54.161 --> 08:56.341
Why don't you at least talk to her?

08:56.341 --> 08:59.271
I mean, I know I should...

09:00.281 --> 09:04.011
Oh, my throat is simply parched.

09:04.381 --> 09:07.541
Surely I saw yellow fruits 
growing along our route.

09:07.541 --> 09:11.771
I know it's awfully selfish of me, 
but I do wish to eat one.

09:11.771 --> 09:13.751
Would you fetch some for me?

09:17.311 --> 09:19.881
All right. I'll go grab them.

09:20.271 --> 09:23.971
I can't approve of you walking 
through the forest alone.

09:23.971 --> 09:28.141
Rudeus, Fitz, kindly accompany her.

09:28.141 --> 09:32.511
<i>I guess she's trying to be considerate?</i>

09:32.931 --> 09:34.081
<i>Still...</i>

09:34.081 --> 09:36.791
Actually, I believe Rudy will be enough.

09:37.541 --> 09:40.031
I will remain at 
Your Royal Highness's side.

09:40.031 --> 09:41.761
Are you certain?

09:41.761 --> 09:43.041
It will be fine.

09:43.041 --> 09:44.791
He won't run away.

09:48.281 --> 09:52.061
<i>Oh, I get it now. 
I have been running away.</i>

09:55.641 --> 09:58.751
<i>But I guess I can't keep 
running forever, huh?</i>

09:59.421 --> 10:02.191
Rudeus, would you mind?

10:04.121 --> 10:05.271
Not at all.

10:18.581 --> 10:21.031
So, you stuck with adventuring.

10:21.481 --> 10:23.241
What's that supposed to mean?

10:24.581 --> 10:27.001
I mean, Counter Arrow broke up,

10:27.001 --> 10:30.701
and Suzanne and Timothy got 
married and quit adventuring.

10:31.051 --> 10:35.461
And Patrice went back to 
Asura to become a soldier.

10:40.691 --> 10:42.611
So, what have you been up to?

10:42.611 --> 10:44.961
I've bounced around from 
one party to another.

10:44.961 --> 10:48.811
But I've been with this one 
ever since I hit rank A.

10:48.811 --> 10:51.851
I've never seen an 
all-women party before.

10:51.851 --> 10:55.351
I think they're pretty 
common at low ranks.

10:55.351 --> 10:59.291
I guess you stop seeing them 
above rank C because people

10:59.291 --> 11:00.971
look for skill over gender.

11:00.971 --> 11:02.361
Huh.

11:02.671 --> 11:05.151
This is the first one I've joined,

11:05.511 --> 11:07.621
but being all women
has a lot of advantages.

11:07.891 --> 11:10.741
Some clients prefer us because 
of it, for one thing.

11:10.741 --> 11:14.861
An all-women party does seem 
perfect for guarding a princess.

11:16.771 --> 11:18.661
Anyway, it's less stressful.

11:18.661 --> 11:21.671
No love-crazed upsets to 
worry about, you know?

11:28.851 --> 11:30.671
But how have <i>you</i> been?

11:31.011 --> 11:32.331
How do you mean?

11:32.331 --> 11:38.931
Suzanne says you're married, have a kid,
 and live happily with your two wives.

11:38.931 --> 11:40.571
Well, I mean...

11:42.051 --> 11:42.911
Sorry.

11:42.911 --> 11:45.501
I'm not looking for an apology!

12:05.231 --> 12:06.321
Sara...

12:06.921 --> 12:10.881
I'm sure you don't want me to 
apologize, but I'm going to.

12:11.711 --> 12:15.471
We didn't exactly part on friendly terms,

12:16.011 --> 12:19.941
so when I suddenly saw you again, 
I didn't know what to say.

12:19.941 --> 12:22.981
But I still shouldn't have ignored you.

12:23.421 --> 12:24.391
Sorry.

12:25.261 --> 12:29.741
I told you, I'm not 
looking for an apology.

12:30.911 --> 12:32.881
Mind if I sit next to you?

12:32.881 --> 12:35.991
You're sure? Your wives won't be happy.

12:35.991 --> 12:39.201
I'll explain as soon as we 
get back with the fruit.

12:39.201 --> 12:43.981
Oh, the princess's bodyguard. 
She's one of them, huh?

12:43.981 --> 12:45.981
Suzanne didn't tell you?

12:45.981 --> 12:48.461
Only that her name's Sylphiette.

12:49.081 --> 12:51.741
But that explains a lot.

12:51.741 --> 12:55.281
Roxy, too. The blue-haired demon.

12:55.281 --> 12:57.021
Huh? Her, too?

12:57.021 --> 12:58.451
Wait, Roxy?

12:58.451 --> 13:00.991
Oh, the one you said taught you magic?

13:00.991 --> 13:02.101
Yeah.

13:02.101 --> 13:03.711
Huh...

13:09.271 --> 13:14.241
You know, I've felt like I owed 
you an apology all this time.

13:14.241 --> 13:16.821
<i>You</i> want to apologize to <i>me?</i>

13:17.151 --> 13:18.201
Yeah.

13:18.201 --> 13:24.071
After we split up, I found out 
the you were, you know, sick.

13:24.851 --> 13:31.501
But I thought I was the only one hurting, 
and I blamed it all on you.

13:35.841 --> 13:38.491
If I'd been more of an adult, 
maybe I would have realized

13:39.071 --> 13:42.181
that I hurt you so badly, 
you wanted to die, too.

13:44.861 --> 13:45.891
Sorry.

13:49.901 --> 13:52.181
I only realized this looking back now,

13:52.771 --> 13:58.461
but I don't think I was actually 
that into you back then.

13:58.461 --> 13:59.731
Oh, yeah?

14:00.381 --> 14:02.481
It goes back to the reason 
for my "condition."

14:02.971 --> 14:07.171
There was this girl called Eris, 
and I thought she'd abandoned me.

14:07.661 --> 14:10.531
And then you were getting 
feelings for me,

14:11.001 --> 14:15.851
so I probably wanted to move 
on and put the past behind me.

14:16.191 --> 14:21.281
But it didn't work out, and I said
 awful things to shield myself.

14:21.921 --> 14:25.021
I wasn't sincere with you.

14:25.801 --> 14:28.581
So, you've got nothing to apologize for.

14:29.131 --> 14:31.611
You've changed.

14:31.611 --> 14:32.781
You think so?

14:32.781 --> 14:37.511
Yeah. The old you would never have 
said that, even if he didn't mean it.

14:37.911 --> 14:41.461
He wouldn't have used such a 
laid-back tone with me, either.

14:41.461 --> 14:47.401
<i>She's right. I did try to keep 
people at arm's length back then.</i>

14:47.721 --> 14:51.161
<i>I was scared of getting hurt 
in the same way again.</i>

14:51.161 --> 14:52.861
<i>I didn't want anyone to hate me.</i>

14:53.381 --> 14:54.621
<i>But now...</i>

14:55.371 --> 14:57.111
I got given confidence.

14:57.601 --> 14:58.891
By your wives?

14:58.891 --> 15:04.401
Yes. Sylphie worked hard 
to cure my condition.

15:05.081 --> 15:09.851
Even though it was her first time, 
she used not just her own body

15:09.851 --> 15:11.861
but aphrodisiacs, too.

15:11.861 --> 15:16.191
Wow. That's, uh, really something.

15:16.731 --> 15:21.451
Wait. You mean you married again 
even after she did all that for you?

15:21.451 --> 15:23.261
It sounds bad, doesn't it?

15:23.851 --> 15:26.501
Roxy did the same thing for me.

15:26.881 --> 15:32.311
When I lost someone important to me, 
and everything seemed pointless,

15:32.311 --> 15:34.021
she saved me.

15:34.511 --> 15:35.541
Oh.

15:38.741 --> 15:41.191
I guess... I couldn't do that.

15:41.691 --> 15:44.981
Probably not even if 
I'd known about your condition.

15:45.651 --> 15:47.191
Maybe that's it.

15:47.191 --> 15:50.331
The reason I couldn't 
get you to fall for me.

15:53.931 --> 15:58.691
<i>She has a point. 
Sylphie and Roxy both still love me.</i>

15:58.691 --> 16:02.241
<i>But I love them both as much or more.</i>

16:02.861 --> 16:06.751
<i>If anything sets them apart from Sara 
and other women, that must be it.</i>

16:11.041 --> 16:13.951
Listen. Don't get the wrong idea!

16:13.951 --> 16:16.481
My feelings for you ended that day!

16:16.481 --> 16:21.821
Yeah, I wanted to apologize because I said
 awful things without knowing your deal,

16:21.821 --> 16:23.101
but that's it!

16:23.101 --> 16:26.631
I don't want to patch things up after 
all this time! Not even a little!

16:27.111 --> 16:31.731
So, don't you look too 
sorry about it, either.

16:32.731 --> 16:36.101
Just treat me like an old comrade.

16:40.551 --> 16:42.801
Sure. Got it.

17:01.311 --> 17:02.271
Roxy!

17:28.011 --> 17:31.071
Will I see Your Highness again?

17:31.071 --> 17:33.871
Yes. Someday.

17:33.871 --> 17:38.481
I wish I had time to learn 
so much more magic from you!

17:38.481 --> 17:39.501
I mean, um...

17:39.501 --> 17:43.271
Oh, we'd love it if you'd join our party!

17:43.271 --> 17:48.761
I appreciate the offer, but I'm satisfied 
with my job, and I have a husband.

17:48.761 --> 17:50.151
Don't worry about him!

17:50.151 --> 17:52.341
You can leave a man for a while,

17:52.341 --> 17:54.971
and he'll just pamper you 
when you finally see him again!

17:54.971 --> 17:57.761
Alyssa! Enough is enough.

17:57.761 --> 17:59.081
Fine.

18:01.581 --> 18:04.571
Well, Rudeus, I guess this is goodbye.

18:04.571 --> 18:06.691
Yeah. Take care.

18:06.691 --> 18:08.131
Same to you.

18:08.131 --> 18:12.531
You seem close with both your wives, 
but you'd better not compare them.

18:12.531 --> 18:15.551
Oh, right. I'll take that to heart.

18:15.551 --> 18:16.921
Great!

18:18.301 --> 18:19.431
See you!

18:29.861 --> 18:33.861
Hey, Rudy, are you sure you should 
have let her go like that?

18:33.861 --> 18:35.241
What do you mean?

18:35.661 --> 18:39.621
You used to like that girl, right?

18:40.491 --> 18:43.781
I... don't think I did.

18:44.261 --> 18:48.241
I was naïve in a lot of ways, 
and I just got a little confused.

18:49.781 --> 18:50.951
Oh, really?

18:53.501 --> 18:56.421
What sort of girl <i>do</i> you like, then?

18:57.541 --> 19:00.201
I... I'd like to know, too!

19:02.771 --> 19:04.381
Let me think...

19:04.851 --> 19:10.081
I guess I get special feelings for girls 
who save me when I'm in a bad place.

19:10.391 --> 19:12.051
Then...

19:13.951 --> 19:15.281
Say, Rudy,

19:15.281 --> 19:18.151
does that mean we're special to you?

19:18.151 --> 19:21.031
Yeah. You're both special.

19:22.711 --> 19:27.031
Special girls who save me when 
I really need it are pretty rare.

19:27.881 --> 19:31.851
So, you've got no reason 
to worry, Sylphie.

19:31.851 --> 19:34.291
I won't be marrying any more wives.

19:34.761 --> 19:35.861
I promise.

19:36.321 --> 19:38.971
Thanks. But you know, Rudy...

19:38.971 --> 19:44.931
If someone is special to you, 
and they feel you're special, too,

19:44.931 --> 19:47.741
I wouldn't have a problem with 
two or three people like that.

19:48.211 --> 19:49.421
Special...

19:52.321 --> 19:54.401
<i>She ditched me.</i>

19:54.861 --> 19:59.931
<i>But Ruijerd told me once that it 
had to be a misunderstanding.</i>

20:02.521 --> 20:03.761
Sylphie.

20:04.211 --> 20:06.031
I can't be certain,

20:06.451 --> 20:09.401
but I may end up
breaking my word again.

20:10.761 --> 20:11.871
That's okay.

20:13.041 --> 20:17.381
But when you do, 
you'd better bring her to us.

20:17.381 --> 20:23.451
I won't put up with someone trying to 
marry you when she doesn't even love you.

20:23.451 --> 20:24.421
Sure.

20:24.771 --> 20:26.681
Promise me that.

20:26.681 --> 20:32.781
If you start seeing someone behind 
my back and spring a kid on me...

20:32.781 --> 20:34.151
Well, even I have my limits.

20:34.151 --> 20:35.691
O-Of course.

20:37.291 --> 20:42.621
In that case, I can't wait to see what 
kind of girl you'll bring home next.

20:44.681 --> 20:48.821
Your technique is already beyond 
the level of a Sword Saint.

20:48.821 --> 20:52.831
I think it's time I chose the 
first Sword King since Ghislaine.

20:52.831 --> 20:54.651
But first, a question.

20:54.651 --> 20:58.031
The Blade of Light is the 
Sword God Style's ultimate technique.

20:58.031 --> 21:01.641
But we still rank the 
people who've learned it.

21:01.641 --> 21:06.121
Sword Saints, Sword Kings, 
Sword Emperors, and the Sword God.

21:06.481 --> 21:08.871
What do you think sets them apart? Gino.

21:09.571 --> 21:14.361
Things apart from techniques. 
Footwork, physical strength, or...

21:14.361 --> 21:16.931
m-maybe how good their weapons are?

21:16.391 --> 21:17.721
Their <i>weapons?!</i>

21:17.921 --> 21:19.751
How many years have you 
been training?!

21:19.751 --> 21:21.821
P-Please forgive me!

21:21.821 --> 21:24.361
Maybe you're still too young to get it.

21:24.361 --> 21:25.671
Well, whatever.

21:25.671 --> 21:28.811
The strong are still strong 
even if you don't know why.

21:28.811 --> 21:31.491
Okay, Nina. Let's hear your answer.

21:32.261 --> 21:33.991
Is it desire?

21:33.991 --> 21:37.911
Ha! I guess you have started 
thinking about boys lately.

21:38.241 --> 21:42.021
So, how much can this 
"desire" of yours take?

21:42.021 --> 21:44.071
What do you mean?

21:44.071 --> 21:45.461
For example,

21:45.461 --> 21:50.431
say I told you to choose between marrying 
Gino and becoming a Sword King.

21:50.431 --> 21:51.551
Which would you choose?

21:53.561 --> 21:55.311
I would choose to become a Sword King.

21:56.251 --> 21:58.831
You never did live in the real world.

21:59.251 --> 22:01.401
Now, Eris. How about you?

22:01.861 --> 22:02.891
Resolve.

22:02.891 --> 22:06.071
Resolve? I don't think so.

22:06.321 --> 22:09.071
I do. It's resolve.

22:09.301 --> 22:12.151
So, you don't care if you 
don't get to be a Sword King?

22:12.151 --> 22:14.081
It wouldn't really bother me.

22:14.081 --> 22:16.121
Don't you want to get stronger?

22:16.121 --> 22:17.871
Yes, I do.

22:18.201 --> 22:20.921
But what does it matter 
what people call me?

22:22.091 --> 22:24.461
Okay. Eris and Nina.

22:24.761 --> 22:28.201
I'll make whichever one 
of you wins a Sword King!

22:30.781 --> 22:34.451
This reminds me of when 
you first got here.

22:34.451 --> 22:35.851
Yes, it does.

22:35.851 --> 22:37.591
Today, I'm going to win.

22:43.381 --> 22:44.861
Rudeus...

22:59.131 --> 23:01.001
How long are you lovebirds 
gonna stare at each other?

23:08.341 --> 23:09.381
That's enough!

23:14.381 --> 23:16.211
Frustrated, Nina?

23:16.891 --> 23:18.101
Yes.

23:18.101 --> 23:19.811
You still have room to grow.

23:20.071 --> 23:21.131
Make the most of it.

23:22.581 --> 23:24.501
Yes, Father...

23:26.501 --> 23:28.071
Well done, Eris.

23:28.771 --> 23:31.361
I grant you the title of Sword King!

23:32.071 --> 23:35.071
<b>Episode 6
Another Domestic Disaster?</b>

23:35.071 --> 23:40.151
Next Time
Phase Four
